+# Navigation entry removals
+
+This fork intentionally hides entries that do not lead to a supported product flow:
+
+- The Settings sidebar does not show `computerUse` / 「电脑控制」 on any platform. The section id, history preference and old navigation intents are retained for compatibility; any remaining intent resolves to `general`. The underlying Computer Use implementation is not deleted, so the entry can be restored by removing `computerUse` from `HIDDEN_SETTINGS_SECTIONS`.
+- The desktop sidebar footer does not render the phone / Web remote-control trigger. The remote-control dialog, host services and mobile `/remote` flow are unchanged; only this desktop entry is removed.
+- The account entry (avatar plus 「连接使用」 / "Connect") is not rendered in either sidebar footer. `WorkspaceSidebarFooter` takes `hideAccountEntry`, and both the project sidebar and the Settings sidebar set it, so the Settings page keeps only its navigation and the back button. The footer account menu was the only place that grouped account identity, logout, locale, theme and zoom; with it gone those controls come from the sections that own the state — model settings owns coding-plan login, and app appearance/language live in 「外观」 and 「常规」. The onboarding flow is unchanged.
+- The sidebar activity slot does not render marketing banners (the seasonal claim-token card). `SidebarBottomActivity` now shows only the highspeed share notice from `GlobalNoticeSurface`. Marketing popups, delivery queries, reporting and the `/mcp`-style surfaces are untouched; restore the banner by rendering `<MarketingBanner />` when `useMarketingBannerVisible()` is true.
+
+Verification: `settingsPageConfig.test.ts` checks the section is absent on desktop and Web and that residual `computerUse` navigation falls back to `general`; `workspaceSidebarFooterWebRemoteControlTooltip.test.ts` checks the footer no longer renders a remote-control trigger and that `hideAccountEntry` drops the account trigger while keeping the settings button; `sidebarBottomActivity.test.ts` checks the slot never renders the marketing banner but still arbitrates highspeed notices.
